wikijs-description =
    Wiki.js is a powerful, fast wiki platform built on Node.js with a clean, modern interface.

    It supports dozens of editor formats including Markdown and WYSIWYG, and stores content
    in a PostgreSQL database with optional Git sync. FreeSynergy ships it pre-configured with
    Kanidm OIDC authentication and optional S3 asset storage.
    It implements the WikiProvider trait — fully interchangeable with Outline.

wikijs-features =
    - Markdown, WYSIWYG, and AsciiDoc editors
    - Full-text search across all pages
    - Hierarchical page structure with breadcrumbs
    - Page history and version comparison
    - OIDC single sign-on via Kanidm
    - SCIM user provisioning from Kanidm
    - Optional S3 storage for file uploads
    - Role-based access control per page and namespace
    - Interchangeable with Outline (same WikiProvider trait)
